(6859060, 1031820, 135744, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by levyj413:</b></div><hr/><i> Fun shot, but what''s strange about the subject or setting? </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>It is a bit of a shoe horn so I was hoping to get away with the big cow looking different from the little cows. Unfortunately there is nothing too unusual about the setting:)</td>', 'Originally posted by levyj413: Fun shot, but what''s strange about the subject or setting?   It is a bit of a shoe horn so I was hoping to get away with the big cow looking different from the little cows. Unfortunately there is nothing too unusual about the setting:)', '2012-09-07 07:25:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(6859061, 1031820, 135744, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by sophiawood:</b></div><hr/><i> Nice pic. I feel like you could do better with this if you changed you composition a bit. The horizon in the center can be pulled off, but I think cropping it off at the bottom may add more focus on your cows. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thank you Sophia - the idea to crop off at the bottom is a great idea and I think it will improve the photo. I think I resisted this thinking it would result in the photo being too "wide-screen". I tend to be really boring and stick to 9x6 or 9x8 in Photoshop with the odd square. Time to get more adventurous:)</td>', 'Originally posted by sophiawood: Nice pic. I feel like you could do better with this if you changed you composition a bit. The horizon in the center can be pulled off, but I think cropping it off at the bottom may add more focus on your cows.   Thank you Sophia - the idea to crop off at the bottom is a great idea and I think it will improve the photo. I think I resisted this thinking it would result in the photo being too "wide-screen". I tend to be really boring and stick to 9x6 or 9x8 in Photoshop with the odd square. Time to get more adventurous:)', '2012-09-07 07:28:05.000000', NULL, 0),
