(6859908, 1031745, 61396, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by posthumous:</b></div><hr/><i> I gave you a 7. I love the capture but I will admit I was distracted by the intense distortion of the wide-angle... the "fisheye" look. I think it overwhelms the shot a bit. But that might just be my bias. It''s a great shot nonetheless. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>wanted the lens choice to deliver a sense of strangeness. Also, it is easier to snap from the hip with a wide angle. Thanks for your generous words (and score).<br/> <br/>p.s. following your comment I have made a less distorted (lens geometry adjusted) version here:<br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=1032998" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/60000-64999/61396/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1032998.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/60000-64999/61396/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1032998.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/60000-64999/61396/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1032998.jpg"/></a> <br/>with warmer colors as a bonus.</td>', 'Originally posted by posthumous: I gave you a 7. I love the capture but I will admit I was distracted by the intense distortion of the wide-angle... the "fisheye" look. I think it overwhelms the shot a bit. But that might just be my bias. It''s a great shot nonetheless.  wanted the lens choice to deliver a sense of strangeness. Also, it is easier to snap from the hip with a wide angle. Thanks for your generous words (and score). p.s. following your comment I have made a less distorted (lens geometry adjusted) version here: with warmer colors as a bonus.', '2012-09-08 08:04:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(6859911, 1031833, 64086, '<td valign="top">Beautiful photo, reminds me of a painting that I love - Umberto Boccioni''s States of Mind III: Those Who Stay.</td>', 'Beautiful photo, reminds me of a painting that I love - Umberto Boccioni''s States of Mind III: Those Who Stay.', '2012-09-08 08:11:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(6859944, 1031388, 64733, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by colorcarnival:</b></div><hr/><i> omg you entered a challenge.  Good to see you again! </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thanks!  I was inspired by my last vacation.  PEI was so nice.  However, not inspired enough to remember to set the clock on the camera.  It''s really discouraging that an amateur gets dq''d for the time on the camera, while trying to compete with real professionals.  And part of the reason I haven''t participated here in over a year.  I find the comments have gotten much less helpful, from a technical perspective, than they used to be.  I would have had a 5.5 on this image, which would have been one of my highest.  <br/> <br/>Oh well, will set the time and play by the rules next time.  I hope DPC finds its way again toward helping people learn and improve their craft.</td>', 'Originally posted by colorcarnival: omg you entered a challenge.  Good to see you again!   Thanks!  I was inspired by my last vacation.  PEI was so nice.  However, not inspired enough to remember to set the clock on the camera.  It''s really discouraging that an amateur gets dq''d for the time on the camera, while trying to compete with real professionals.  And part of the reason I haven''t participated here in over a year.  I find the comments have gotten much less helpful, from a technical perspective, than they used to be.  I would have had a 5.5 on this image, which would have been one of my highest.   Oh well, will set the time and play by the rules next time.  I hope DPC finds its way again toward helping people learn and improve their craft.', '2012-09-08 09:28:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(6859972, 1031316, 122678, '<td valign="top">littlemav I''m with you! (I thought the scars were real!)<br/>I live in NY and work in the city. A glass blower in this area is an oddity. How ever, I did go to a strange festival with strange people from strange places and this man had an unusual craft. I did go there to see what I could capture, so I did feel it met the challenge and quite well. i am more of a documentary photographer, sorry not everyone could see the challenge, I will try harder next time. Thank you for taking the time to view and write. <br/>:D</td>', 'littlemav I''m with you! (I thought the scars were real!)I live in NY and work in the city. A glass blower in this area is an oddity. How ever, I did go to a strange festival with strange people from strange places and this man had an unusual craft. I did go there to see what I could capture, so I did feel it met the challenge and quite well. i am more of a documentary photographer, sorry not everyone could see the challenge, I will try harder next time. Thank you for taking the time to view and write. :D', '2012-09-08 10:08:18.000000', NULL, 0),
